  "identifier": "default",
  "description": "The app's own views — the main window, other windows of the same folder, and the notes popped out of them — and nothing else: the core's commands, window focus, closing its own window once its tabs are saved, and the window's zoom (ADR 0072, revised 2026-10-20), and the window controls a window without the system's title bar draws itself — dragging, minimizing, maximizing, closing (ADR 0072) — and the system's notifications, asked for and sent, while the window is not in front (ADR 0084 item 9). Listed by web view, not by window, so a web page shown inside a window (a child view labelled web-*) gets none of it. No fs plugin and no dialog permission: notes are reached only through verso-core, and the native folder picker runs on the host's side (pick_folder), so no path ever reaches the UI (ADR 0026 rule 4).",
